# This gitignore is a whitelist. Inspired by https://rgbcu.be/blog/gitignore
#
# Everything is ignored, then specific things are re-included.
#
# "!*/" is load-bearing. The "*" pattern matches directories too, and git does
# not descend into an ignored directory, so without "!*/" none of the re-includes
# below can ever match a file inside a subdirectory (tests/, .github/workflows/).

*
!*/

!.gitignore

!*.md
!*.py
!*.toml
!*.yml

!Dockerfile
!config.yaml
!docker-compose.yaml
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt

# Re-ignored below. Now that git descends into subdirectories, these have to be
# excluded explicitly or their contents would match the re-includes above.
# A virtualenv is the dangerous one: it is full of .py files.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Secrets and local state
.env
.env.*
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
